Vendored con-leche
------------------

Most of Ix/Kernel is a modified copy of con-leche, the verified Lean kernel
checker at https://github.com/leanprover/con-leche, vendored in place:

  * the files of con-leche's ConLeche/ tree that the certified checker uses,
    at revision ae0c0c4e4ce6a0081648aff03fe9c39d002c4526, and seven of them
    at revision 3ca9e2fe749a51cba4c6e3527aeecba074c29316 (upstream task
    #323), received under the Apache License, Version 2.0; con-leche's
    licence is LICENSE-CON-LECHE in this directory;
  * every such file was changed: scripts/vendor-conleche.py moves it from
    ConLeche/Kernel/X or ConLeche/X to Ix/Kernel/X, renames the namespace
    and module prefix ConLeche to Ix.Kernel, and adds a first line naming
    its source file and this notice. A file with that line has no other
    change;
  * seven files carry further changes, each listed in its own header
    ("Ported from con-leche at ..."): CheckerBase.lean, Level.lean,
    MainTheorem.lean, Frontend/InModel/Nested.lean, Verify/Level.lean and
    Verify/Cached/{AgreeFloor,PushChain}.lean;
  * LevelGeran.lean and Verify/LevelGeran.lean, inside the vendored tree,
    and Ref.lean, Search.lean and the Audit, Ingress, Egress and Ixon
    directories, beside it, are this repository's (Ref.lean as below).

Each file's source path, revision and SHA-256, and its own SHA-256, are
recorded in Tests/Ix/Kernel/ImportManifest.lean; lake exe kernel-provenance
checks them, and with --source-git re-derives every rewritten file from
upstream. Upstream holds the copyright of the con-leche files; the changes
are Argument Computer Corporation's, under the same licence.

The old Ix branch
-----------------

Ix/Kernel/Ref.lean was ported from the jcb/ix-kernel-consistency branch of
the Ix repository (revision ad60e5f6dd23655da79cf9898d2b6b3fefbe8658,
directory Ix/Theory). There it was authored in the Lean4Ix working tree,
and Lean4Ix is based on lean4lean:

  https://github.com/digama0/lean4lean

The lean4lean-derived portions were received under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. Their original copyright, attribution, licensing, and
modification-notice requirements continue to apply. The repository history
and retained per-file notices provide the detailed provenance of those
portions.

The rest of that port, the intrinsic kernel's model and certified
constructions, was retired on 2026-10-01 (step L6 of
plans/ix-kernel-con-leche-port-v4.md). It included Ix/Kernel/Model/SetTheory
and Ix/Kernel/Model/SetModel, a port of the con-leche set-theoretic
foundation received under the Apache License, Version 2.0, from
https://github.com/leanprover/con-leche at revision
86cd20a65660d757cedc81561a44579099b565d0. The repository history retains
those files and their notices. The certified checker now uses con-leche's
own set theory, vendored as above (Ix/Kernel/SetTheory, Ix/Kernel/SetModel).

In the Lean4Ix tree, certain files also identify more specific Apache-2.0
sources in their headers; none of these files is part of this repository:

  * Main.lean contains code copied from leanprover-community/import-graph.
  * Lean4Lean/Std/ToExpr.lean contains code from mathlib.
  * Lean4Lean/Verify/QSort.lean is adapted from Lean 4's qsort verification.

Lean 4, Batteries, import-graph, and mathlib are distributed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. When a distribution of this code includes their code
or artifacts, preserve the license and notice material shipped with them.

The exact source and ported file hashes are recorded in
Tests/Ix/Kernel/ImportManifest.lean and checked by
Tests/Ix/Kernel/Provenance.lean (lake exe kernel-provenance).

Except where a contribution or upstream component is explicitly identified
under different terms, contributions intentionally submitted for inclusion
in Ix/Kernel are accepted under the same MIT OR Apache-2.0 choice described
in LICENSE, LICENSE-MIT, and LICENSE-APACHE in this directory.

